{"id":"mahabharata-3-210","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":210,"title":"दशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 210 · The fires of Kashyapa's line","summary":{"en":"Markandeya continues with the fire Pancajanya, born of the austerities of Kashyapa, Vasishtha and others, and the many fires descended from him, including those that steal the sacrifice and the fire Rathantara.","kn":"ಕಾಶ್ಯಪ, ವಸಿಷ್ಠ ಮೊದಲಾದವರ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ಪಾಂಚಜನ್ಯ ಅಗ್ನಿಯನ್ನೂ, ಯಜ್ಞವನ್ನು ಕದಿಯುವ ಅಗ್ನಿಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ರಥಂತರ ಅಗ್ನಿ ಸೇರಿದಂತೆ ಅವನಿಂದ ಬಂದ ಅನೇಕ ಅಗ್ನಿಗಳನ್ನೂ ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ಮುಂದುವರಿಸಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"मार्कण्डेय कश्यप, वसिष्ठ आदि के तप से उत्पन्न पाञ्चजन्य अग्नि और उससे उत्पन्न अनेक अग्नियों का वर्णन जारी रखते हैं, जिनमें यज्ञ चुराने वाली अग्नियाँ और रथन्तर अग्नि भी हैं।","te":"కాశ్యపుడు, వసిష్ఠుడు మొదలైనవారి తపస్సుతో పుట్టిన పాంచజన్య అగ్నిని, యజ్ఞాన్ని దొంగిలించే అగ్నులు, రథంతర అగ్ని సహా అతని నుండి వచ్చిన అనేక అగ్నులను మార్కండేయుడు కొనసాగించి వివరిస్తాడు.","ta":"காஶ்யபர், வஸிஷ்டர் முதலியோரின் தவத்தால் பிறந்த பாஞ்சஜன்ய அக்னியையும், யாகத்தைத் திருடும் அக்னிகள், ரதந்தர அக்னி உட்பட அவனிடமிருந்து தோன்றிய பல அக்னிகளையும் மார்க்கண்டேயர் தொடர்ந்து விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"കശ്യപന്റെയും വസിഷ്ഠന്റെയും മറ്റുള്ളവരുടെയും തപസ്സിൽനിന്ന് ജനിച്ച പഞ്ചജന്യൻ എന്ന അഗ്നിയെ മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ തുടർന്ന് വിവരിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിൽനിന്ന് ഇറങ്ങിയ പല അഗ്നികളും, യാഗഹവിസ്സ് മോഷ്ടിക്കുന്നവയും, രഥന്തരം എന്ന അഗ്നിയും ഉൾപ്പെടെ."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.210; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"काश्यपो ह्यथ वासिष्ठः प्राणश्च प्राणपुत्रकः ।\nअग्निराङ्गिरसश्चैव च्यवनस्त्रिषुवर्चकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kashyapa, Vasishtha, Prana and his son, Angiras's fire, and Chyavana, Trishuvarchaka, those sages...\""}},{"n":2,"text":"अचरन्त तपस्तीव्रं पुत्रार्थे बहुवार्षिकम् ।\nपुत्रं लभेम धर्मिष्ठं यशसा ब्रह्मणा समम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"practiced harsh austerity for many years for the sake of a son, saying: 'May we gain a most righteous son, equal to Brahma in glory.'\""}},{"n":3,"text":"महाव्याहृतिभिर्ध्यातः पञ्चभिस्तैस्तदा त्वथ ।\nजज्ञे तेजोमयोऽर्चिष्मान्पञ्चवर्णः प्रभावनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, as they meditated on the five great utterances, there was born a shining, fiery, five-colored being of great power.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"समिद्धोऽग्निः शिरस्तस्य बाहू सूर्यनिभौ तथा ।\nत्वङ्नेत्रे च सुवर्णाभे कृष्णे जङ्घे च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"His head was a kindled fire; his arms were like the sun; his skin and eyes were golden; and his legs were dark, descendant of Bharata.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"पञ्चवर्णः स तपसा कृतस्तैः पञ्चभिर्जनैः ।\nपाञ्चजन्यः श्रुतो वेदे पञ्चवंशकरस्तु सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Made five-colored by the austerity of those five men, he was known in the Veda as Panchajanya, the founder of five lines.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"दश वर्षसहस्राणि तपस्तप्त्वा महातपाः ।\nजनयत्पावकं घोरं पितॄणां स प्रजाः सृजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"After practicing austerity for ten thousand years, that great ascetic produced a terrible fire and began creating offspring for the ancestors.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"बृहद्रथंतरं मूर्ध्नो वक्त्राच्च तरसाहरौ ।\nशिवं नाभ्यां बलादिन्द्रं वाय्वग्नी प्राणतोऽसृजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From his head he made Brihat and Rathantara; from his mouth, swiftly, Hari; from his navel Shiva; from his strength Indra; and from his breath Vayu and Agni.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"बाहुभ्यामनुदात्तौ च विश्वे भूतानि चैव ह ।\nएतान्सृष्ट्वा ततः पञ्च पितॄणामसृजत्सुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From his arms he made the two Anudattas and the Vishvedevas and beings. Having made these, he then created five sons of the ancestors.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"बृहदूर्जस्य प्रणिधिः काश्यपस्य बृहत्तरः ।\nभानुरङ्गिरसो वीरः पुत्रो वर्चस्य सौभरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Pranidhi was of Brihadurja, Brihattara of Kashyapa, brave Bhanu of Angiras, and Saubhara was the son of Varchas.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"प्राणस्य चानुदात्तश्च व्याख्याताः पञ्च वंशजाः ।\nदेवान्यज्ञमुषश्चान्यान्सृजन्पञ्चदशोत्तरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Anudatta was Prana's son. Thus the five born in the line are told. Creating further, he made fifteen more, thieves of the sacrifice, to be gods.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अभीममतिभीमं च भीमं भीमबलाबलम् ।\nएतान्यज्ञमुषः पञ्च देवानभ्यसृजत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Abhima, Atibhima, Bhima, Bhimabala and Abala: through austerity he created these five sacrifice-stealing gods.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"सुमित्रं मित्रवन्तं च मित्रज्ञं मित्रवर्धनम् ।\nमित्रधर्माणमित्येतान्देवानभ्यसृजत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sumitra, Mitravat, Mitrajna, Mitravardhana and Mitradharman: through austerity he created these gods.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"सुरप्रवीरं वीरं च सुकेशं च सुवर्चसम् ।\nसुराणामपि हन्तारं पञ्चैतानसृजत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surapravira, Vira, Sukesha, Suvarchas and Surahantri: he created these five by austerity.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"त्रिविधं संस्थिता ह्येते पञ्च पञ्च पृथक्पृथक् ।\nमुष्णन्त्यत्र स्थिता ह्येते स्वर्गतो यज्ञयाजिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These are established in three groups of five each. Stationed here, they steal from those who sacrifice for the sake of heaven.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"तेषामिष्टं हरन्त्येते निघ्नन्ति च महद्भुवि ।\nस्पर्धया हव्यवाहानां निघ्नन्त्येते हरन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They carry off the offerings meant for those performers and strike great harm on earth. In rivalry with the offering-bearing fires they strike and steal.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"हविर्वेद्यां तदादानं कुशलैः संप्रवर्तितम् ।\nतदेते नोपसर्पन्ति यत्र चाग्निः स्थितो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The skilled have arranged for the offering to be taken up on the altar. These beings do not approach where a fire is stationed.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"चितोऽग्निरुद्वहन्यज्ञं पक्षाभ्यां तान्प्रबाधते ।\nमन्त्रैः प्रशमिता ह्येते नेष्टं मुष्णन्ति यज्ञियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The piled fire carries the sacrifice and holds them off with its two wings. Quelled by mantras, they do not steal the sacrificial offering.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"बृहदुक्थतपस्यैव पुत्रो भूमिमुपाश्रितः ।\nअग्निहोत्रे हूयमाने पृथिव्यां सद्भिरिज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brihaduktha, the son of Tapas, rests on the earth. When the agnihotra is offered, good men worship him on earth.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"रथंतरश्च तपसः पुत्रोऽग्निः परिपठ्यते ।\nमित्रविन्दाय वै तस्य हविरध्वर्यवो विदुः ।\nमुमुदे परमप्रीतः सह पुत्रैर्महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The fire Rathantara is also recited as a son of Tapas. Adhvaryus know that his offering is for Mitravinda. Of great fame, he rejoiced, extremely pleased, with his sons.\""}}]}]}